---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';

const app = appBySlug('recart')!;
const path = '/apps/recart';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'apps/recart');
const desc = description(site, 'apps/recart');

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Is Recart currently Messenger first?",
    "answer": "Current supplier material emphasizes SMS, list growth and managed service. Messenger remains listed as an integration; that does not prove a new account supports every historical Messenger automation. Confirm any legacy use case directly."
  },
  {
    "question": "What does managed SMS mean here?",
    "answer": "Recart advertises a dedicated customer success manager and help with strategy, testing and campaigns. Agree who drafts, approves, schedules and pauses sends, and who handles shopper replies."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is email capture an email delivery suite?",
    "answer": "No. Growing an email list is distinct from sending email journeys. Establish where captured records go, which permission fields travel with them and which sender delivers lifecycle email."
  },
  {
    "question": "How much does Recart cost?",
    "answer": "The Shopify listing shows a $299 monthly Starter and free migration/onboarding. The website has several packages and commitments. Obtain a complete quote for the selected service, usage, fees and term."
  },
  {
    "question": "Do I need another popup app?",
    "answer": "Only if a real capture requirement is missing. Recart offers native popups and OneClick list growth. Test that path before adding another form and synchronization dependency."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should I compare Postscript?",
    "answer": "Use identical capture, purchaser suppression and reply cases. Compare service responsibilities and full quotes with matching destinations and message mix. Neither brand is a universal winner."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can browse reminders reach everyone?",
    "answer": "Do not assume so. A usable identity, required permission and supported event are inputs. Test a consented visitor, an anonymous visitor and a later purchaser before enabling the journey."
  },
  {
    "question": "Must Recart run with Sequenzy?",
    "answer": "No. Retain an email sender that meets your needs. Coordinate capture destinations, permissions and cart suppression across whichever systems you choose."
  },
  {
    "question": "What is the launch gate?",
    "answer": "Approve capture and offer behavior, verify purchaser suppression, establish reply and service ownership, and confirm the complete quote. A fixed order threshold or trial length cannot replace these checks."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/apps">All app reviews</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{app.name} review for Shopify stores</h1>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Current offering and review scope</h2>
      <p>Recart currently markets SMS and list growth for Shopify with managed help. This is a supplier-document review and set of proposed exercises, not an account of beauty, streetwear or home-goods trials. The decision is whether its capture flow and service arrangement can run your approved SMS program.</p>
      <p><a href="https://apps.shopify.com/recart">Recart’s Shopify listing</a> describes managed SMS, email and text capture, automation and click attribution. The <a href="https://recart.com/">current website</a> centers SMS, OneClick popups and list growth. Reviewed November 25, 2026; supplier descriptions are not performance evidence.</p>
      <p>Facebook Messenger remains in the integration field. That is narrower than proof that historical Messenger cart flows are sold and supported for new accounts. For an old installation, ask which flows, audiences and exports remain available. Messenger subscribers are not automatically SMS-consented contacts.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Managed service handoff</h2>
      <p>Recart advertises a dedicated CSM and managed strategy, testing and campaigns. Request a sample approval cycle: who proposes the audience, checks exclusions, writes the offer, signs off and schedules the send. Put revision turnaround and emergency pause ownership in the agreement.</p>
      <p>The marketing service may not operate customer support. Assign a merchant reply owner and specify inbox destination, coverage and required access. Rehearse a handoff when the CSM is unavailable. A shared planning channel does not establish that shopper replies are monitored.</p>
      <p>Keep product facts, incentive limits, brand language and prohibited promises in a versioned brief. Require approval when an AI-assisted campaign changes an offer or product claim. Service ownership should reduce work while leaving decisions traceable.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Capture exercise: one tap and separate permissions</h2>
      <p>Start with Recart’s native popup and OneClick offering before buying another capture tool. Test a recognized returning shopper and a first-time visitor on a phone. Record what each sees and which fields are stored after completion.</p>
      <p>For a beauty welcome incentive, inspect email and SMS permission separately. Repeat with an existing opt-out, a mistyped phone and a visitor who closes the second step. Check that the incentive promised in the popup is the one delivered in the welcome flow.</p>
      <p>Measure impressions, completed steps, usable records and delivery failures using consistent eligibility rules. Popup clicks alone are not subscribers, and supplier list-growth percentages are not a forecast for your store.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Shopify and email integration boundaries</h2>
      <p>Follow a staff record from capture into Recart and the selected email sender. Compare identity, source, permission status, timestamp and incentive code. Decide which system is authoritative when records disagree and test opt-out propagation.</p>
      <p>Inspect cart variant, quantity, link, event time and purchase suppression. Test a guest who buys with a different email but the same phone. Put unresolved identity cases in an exception queue rather than assuming every checkout joins safely.</p>
      <p>Recart promotes journeys beyond carts, including welcome and replenishment. For subscription or loyalty conditions, demonstrate the actual field, freshness and missing-value behavior. Collecting email is distinct from operating an email delivery suite.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Pricing package and commitment</h2>
      <p>The Shopify listing shows Starter at $299 monthly and a free state for migration and onboarding. The <a href="https://recart.com/sms-marketing-pricing-ecommerce">supplier pricing page</a> presents several package and commitment tables, including list-growth and combined SMS offerings. Obtain the exact package, term and usage schedule together.</p>
      <p>Ask which allowance, SMS/MMS rates, carrier fees, verification charges and managed tasks apply. Confirm renewal, cancellation and number migration terms. Free onboarding does not establish free ongoing sends.</p>
      <p>Price ordinary and sale-week cohorts with actual copy, destinations and images, including multipart messages. Separate cash costs from staff hours genuinely replaced by the service. A managed package and bare software rate do different work, so compare their complete scope.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Proposed exercise: beauty cart and discount boundaries</h2>
      <p>Create a $64 staff cart. Prepare a no-discount reminder and optional later 15% offer as a proposed test, not a universal sequence. Purchase before the offer and confirm suppression. Repeat with an excluded product, sale item and expired code.</p>
      <p>The example 15% reduction costs $9.60 before shipping subsidy. Check stacking with the welcome incentive and repeat redemption. The merchant approves discount limits; a managed workflow should not escalate the offer merely because another touch is available.</p>
      <p>Change inventory before opening the reminder. Check the cart and approved fallback. Do not promise an item is reserved or available without a demonstrated stock check.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Proposed exercise: social visitor to welcome flow</h2>
      <p>Land on a skincare page from an Instagram campaign link. Complete current SMS capture and inspect source tracking, permission and the welcome offer. Repeat on desktop and a recognized returning device.</p>
      <p>This evaluates the current capture path rather than assuming social visitors should enter Messenger. If a legacy Messenger flow matters, obtain account-specific confirmation and rehearse it separately before allocating budget.</p>
      <p>Test accepting email while declining SMS. The email record should reach its intended sender without a marketing text. Ask the service team to report partial completion so it is visible in the acquisition funnel.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Proposed exercise: browse and later purchase</h2>
      <p>On a consented staff account, view several streetwear products without adding to cart. Have the implementer demonstrate the supported browse trigger and eligibility conditions. Repeat anonymously and after opt-out; those visitors should not silently become reachable SMS subscribers.</p>
      <p>Purchase before the reminder and change stock on a browsed variant. Inspect exclusion and destination behavior. Do not assert inventory-aware recommendations until demonstrated; an approved collection page may be a more durable fallback for a disappearing drop.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Proposed exercise: replies and order permission</h2>
      <p>Reply to a home-goods reminder with a delivery-date question, then ask to change an address on a placed order. Identify the inbox, support owner and visible history. Test a weekend reply and agent transfer.</p>
      <p>Marketing management does not confer order-edit authority. An authorized support operator must verify identity before promising an address edit or refund. Specify which tasks Recart’s service performs and which return to the merchant.</p>
      <p>For replenishment and review journeys, rehearse gift and partial-fulfillment cases. Inspect the timing signal and competing messages from other apps. Keep unaccepted journeys disabled rather than assuming every template fits.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Launch and service acceptance</h2>
      <p>Inventory the old sender, forms and scheduled campaigns. Preserve permission evidence and agree number porting or provisioning steps with both providers. Record the last send and queued messages, pause the duplicate journey and test inbound replies after enabling the replacement.</p>
      <p>Begin with the accepted cohort and agreed budget cap. Review rejected imports, event delays and reply exceptions with the CSM before expanding. A mandatory three-week overlap is not a safe default when equivalent automations could duplicate sends.</p>
      <p>Keep email with the sender meeting your requirements while validating capture synchronization. A new SMS service does not compel an email migration or second popup tool.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Contribution versus click attribution</h2>
      <p>The listing advertises seven-day-click attribution. Treat it as a defined reporting view, not proof of incrementality. Deduplicate order IDs against Shopify, subtract refunds and reconcile credits from other senders.</p>
      <p>Hypothetical planning: 20 additional orders at $32 contribution each yield $640 before program costs. An assumed complete program cost of $500 leaves $140; a $700 cost loses $60 at the same lift. These are calculation inputs, not a Recart quote or measured result.</p>
      <p>Include discounts, shipping subsidy and remaining merchant labor in contribution. Separate capture effects from SMS where feasible: someone acquired by a popup may later buy through email. Report cohort sizes and uncertainty rather than crediting every recovered order to the newest tool.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Weekly review and exit readiness</h2>
      <p>Review the audience, offer, estimated bill and approval record with the CSM. The merchant owner verifies exclusions and staff coverage. After sending, reconcile usable subscribers, failed deliveries, replies, opt-outs, billed usage and deduplicated orders.</p>
      <p>Keep settings, permission exports and approvals accessible to the merchant. Rehearse pausing sends or transferring the number if service ownership changes. Choose managed SMS for demonstrated work and economics, not a fixed order threshold or historical Messenger recovery percentage.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card"><h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Related reading</h2><ul>
      <li><a class="link" href="/apps">apps</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="/apps/postscript">apps · postscript</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">use cases · abandoned cart</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="/apps/sequenzy">apps · sequenzy</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-postscript">compare · klaviyo vs postscript</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="/apps/smsbump">apps · smsbump</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="/apps/firepush">apps · firepush</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="/for/fashion">for · fashion</a></li>
    </ul></div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Recart Shopify FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
